sentences.text:
The present petition has been preferred for the following reliefs:-
(i) for directing the respondent authorities to reinstate the possession of the petitioner to his private land i.e. reyati land bearing khesra no. 230 & 231 having in detail and clearly mentioned in schedule no.2 of registered partition deed;
(ii) for directing the respondents to Patna High Court CWJC No.10136 of 2020(20) dt.11-03-2024 remove the pucca construction of PCC road from the land of the petitioner and to reinstate it peacefully;
(iii) for direction upon respondent for removal of construction of public road on the private land of the petitioner by intrusion upon the same by government authorities under CM scheme of Saat Nischay Yojna;
Upendra Narayan Singh vs The State Of Bihar on 11 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198794531/
1

(iv) for direction upon respondent to either removal of constructed road on petitioners land or for adequate payment of compensation under law, for which no written consent was taken by the respondents from the petitioner nor the due process of law was followed i.e. no land was acquired under the land acquisition act nor adequate compensation was paid to petitioner;
(v) for direction to all the respondent nos. to act upon and co-operate with the petitioner and after going through the documents if required related to the land bearing Khata No. 100, 101, Khesra No.
230 and 231, Thana no. 331, hand over the land as earlier i.e. before construction of Patna High Court CWJC No.10136 of 2020(20) dt.11-03-2024 present PCC road to the petitioner.

respectively shall file separate affidavits on:
(i) whether the land on which the investment has been made exclusively belongs to the petitioner and his agnates/respondents or it is being used by the local villagers and the road moves ahead to the houses of local villagers too;
Upendra Narayan Singh vs The State Of Bihar on 11 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198794531/
2 (ii) if the land is being used exclusively by the Patna High Court CWJC No.10136 of 2020(20) dt.11-03-2024 families of the petitioner and the respondent no. 9, how the Saat Nischay Yojana was extended on the private land and money invested;
(iii) what is the amount that has been invested under the Saat Nischay Yojana on the said private land;
(iv) copy of the Saat Nischay Yojana be also annexed to show exactly what is the scheme and whether it includes of investment of Government money on a private land too.
10.

